{
  "title": "Discoid Meniscus",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/knee-and-sports/3007/discoid-meniscus",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 7 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "A discoid meniscus is the abnormal development of the meniscus leading to a hypertrophic and discoid shaped meniscus.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be suspected on radiographs with (squaring of lateral condyle with cupping of lateral tibial plateau) but require MRI for confirmation **(**3 or more 5mm sagittal images with meniscal continuity).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is generally observation for patients who are asymptomatic. Arthroscopic meniscectomy and saucerization may be indicated for patients with continued pain and mechanical symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "common",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "present in 3-5% of population",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually lateral **meniscus** involved",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**25% bilateral**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "failure of apoptosis in utero",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
